{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Ms. Brooks. Let me address each of your questions. First, regarding the roster reduction from ten to eight — I don't yet have a recommendation on which two students would be cut. I think we should establish clear criteria, such as skill level, attendance reliability, and commitment to the full season, and I'd welcome Ms. Carter's input on any scheduling or availability factors that should inform those criteria, especially given what she's shared about Jordan's constraints. Second, regarding the wired network requirement — to meet the league standard, we would need Ethernet switches and sufficient Cat5 or Cat6 cabling to connect all match stations to a local wired network rather than relying on the school's Wi-Fi. I'd need to assess what equipment the school already has and what we'd need to purchase or borrow, and I'd want to confirm the room we'd use has enough wired network ports or capacity for switches. Third, on the interaction between the roster and scheduling issues — since the league requires exactly eight students and allows five active players per match, we have some flexibility: even if Jordan can't attend weekend tournaments, we could still field five active players from the remaining seven, as long as the other seven are available. That said, we'd want to make sure we have reliable attendance from enough students for each match. I'd suggest we finalize the roster criteria together and I'll prepare a wired-network equipment estimate before Friday's meeting."}
